>
<p>An ecommerce website audit examines how shoppers and search engines move through a product catalogue. The scope should define platforms, markets, product and category samples, checkout permissions and available commercial data.</p>
<p>AuditWeb quotes ecommerce work after reviewing catalogue size, faceted navigation, templates, integrations and deliverables. The service does not promise a revenue uplift.</p>

<h2 id="ecommerce-audit-challenges">What makes an ecommerce audit different?</h2>
<p>Ecommerce audits must account for product states, variants, filters, pagination, currency and transactional pages. A representative sample should include best-selling, low-stock, discontinued and variant products where those states exist.</p>
<p>Google provides specific guidance for <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/crawling-indexing/crawling-managing-faceted-navigation">faceted navigation URLs</a>. The correct control depends on whether filtered URLs need to appear in search. The audit should record that decision before recommending robots or canonical changes.</p>

<h2 id="product-page-review">What should product and category reviews cover?</h2>
<p>The review should test templates and real instances. Product evidence can include titles, descriptions, images, availability, variants, internal links and rendered structured data.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Product pages:</strong> compare visible product data with metadata and structured data.</li>
  <li><strong>Category pages:</strong> review indexable value, pagination, filters and product discovery.</li>
  <li><strong>Product states:</strong> document how unavailable and replaced products behave.</li>
  <li><strong>Variants:</strong> record URL, canonical and selection behaviour for actual examples.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="checkout-flow">How should checkout be reviewed?</h2>
<p>Checkout review needs explicit permission and a test plan. Define devices, accounts, payment method, delivery location and whether the auditor may place or cancel an order.</p>
<p>The report can record navigation, validation, errors and performance on the agreed journey. It should not claim payment security or legal compliance from a visual check.</p>

<h2 id="site-speed">How should ecommerce performance be measured?</h2>
<p>Measure representative product, category and checkout templates separately. Record whether evidence comes from real-user field data or a controlled lab run.</p>
<p>Google defines good Core Web Vitals using LCP, INP and CLS at the 75th percentile in its <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/core-web-vitals">Core Web Vitals guidance</a>. A single lab test cannot establish a site's field classification.</p>

<h2 id="schema-and-rich-results">What product structured data should the audit check?</h2>
<p>The audit should compare visible product information with rendered Product data and Google's required properties. Markup must describe the page accurately.</p>
<p>Google distinguishes product snippets from merchant listings and documents price, availability, shipping and return information in its <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/product">Product structured data documentation</a>. Valid markup creates eligibility rather than guaranteed rich results.</p>

<h2 id="whats-included">What does the ecommerce audit deliver?</h2>
<p>The deliverable records scope, samples, evidence, findings, fixes and verification steps. Agree whether the package also includes exports, stakeholder presentation or implementation workshop.</p>
<p>Use the <a href="/website-audit-services/report-example/">report example</a> to compare evidence fields. Use the <a href="/website-audit-checklist/ecommerce/">ecommerce audit checklist</a> to prepare the initial scope.</p>

<h2 id="pricing">How much does an ecommerce audit cost?</h2>
<p>Ecommerce audits use a custom quote because catalogue size, platforms, filters, checkout testing, markets and integrations change the work materially. Provide those details with the enquiry.</p>
<p>The general $297 basic and $997 comprehensive prices describe AuditWeb's standard website audits. AuditWeb confirms whether either scope fits only after reviewing the store. Implementation and outcome measurement are separate.</p>
